model {
  extend basalt.deployment {
    metadata {
      constraint "The pool image publication receipt is not memoized, so each sequential release phase rewrites it inside the runner's private mkdtemp directory. Post-deploy image verification proves the root application first. Only when the root has zero running instances and the PoolWorker binds a blue/green fleet does it verify the fleet instead: each bound application once against its own immutable configured digest, and at least one running instance in an application whose image input equals POOL_DESIRED_IMAGE_INPUT. Each missing, malformed, foreign, duplicate or stale fact refuses with the exact binding or field. Recorded recovery reads no Worker bindings and never substitutes a fleet for its exact old container. The read-only Check probe runs the same verifier against the native production baseline whenever the verifier or its probe changes. The release deploy job allows 180 minutes so that a healthy multi-phase release is never cancelled between an upload and its activation."
    }
  }
}
